From f597ae36806e5406d4763ee77132cb1be16f74fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yankneck696 <yankneck696@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PlutoSDR: RX2 as a second aerial or PureSignal feedback
 for the RX1 radio (#525)

Adapted from the LimeSDR-USB's second-chain support: PlutoConfig gains aux,
the same block a LimeSDR's second chain uses (PlutoAuxConfig is
LimeAuxConfig), and src/pluto_source.rs follows src/lime_source.rs, borrowing
RX2 into the RX1 radio and feeding it to the shared sdroxide_dsp::Diversity
(Cancel/Combine, driven from the main window's DIV strip) or
sdroxide_dsp::PureSignal. PureSignal needs full duplex, since the coupler is
only heard while receive keeps running through the over. Wire protocol v187,
because the radio configuration crosses whole.

Both chains arrive in one 2R2T device buffer. The receive thread commits each
buffer to both chains' rings or to neither, recording where chain 1 starts in
chain 0's count, so PlutoRx::rx_read_paired hands over the two chains'
samples of the same instants. PlutoRig::aux_rx borrows chain 1 that way, and
a loopback test covers the pairing.

Over Ethernet the transmission comes back on RX2 a few hundred milliseconds
after it was predistorted (host ring, DMA buffers both ways, the network
twice), well past the tenth of a second PureSignal::new keeps.
PureSignal::with_history takes a longer history, and while unlocked the
delay search runs eight times a second rather than on every block, so the
longer history costs nothing extra. The Pluto uses one second and unlocks at
each key-up. A test covers a delay the default history cannot reach.

Diversity (Cancel) tried on a PlutoSky R2. PureSignal is not yet verified on
hardware: the receive stalls of #719 break its feedback stream.
